# Build output and caches
.gradle/
build/
run/
out/
bin/

# IDE. bin/ above is the VS Code Java extension's output directory; these
# are the rest of what that extension and Eclipse drop into a project.
# NOTE gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar is deliberately NOT ignored: it
# is a tracked part of the wrapper and a clone cannot build without it.
.idea/
.vscode/
.project
.classpath
.settings/
.factorypath
*.iml

# JVM crash and profiling artifacts. This project runs real Minecraft
# clients constantly, and a crashed JVM writes these next to the working
# directory. A heap dump is hundreds of megabytes, so accidentally
# committing one is not a small mistake.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
.attach_pid*
*.hprof
*.log

# Machine-local configuration. Anything whose value is a path on one
# person's disk belongs here rather than in build.gradle: shipping such a
# path is exactly what stopped a clean clone from building before 1.0.0.
local.properties

# Operating system clutter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local tooling
__pycache__/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
